
The recognizer will be trained when the application starts. If no
`known_faces/` directory exists, detection still works but every face is
labeled `Unknown`.

## Troubleshooting

### `error: externally-managed-environment`

This error occurs when you try to install Python packages with a Python
installation that your operating system manages (e.g., the system Python
on Debian/Ubuntu). To avoid this, always use the project’s virtual
environment:

- The simplest way is to run `make install`, which creates `.venv/` and
  installs everything inside it.
- If you already have a `.venv/` directory, activate it first:

  ```bash
  source .venv/bin/activate
  pip install -r requirements.txt
  ```

- Never use `--break-system-packages` unless you know exactly what you are
  doing—it can damage your system Python.
